Z||000002||WisconsinGT||01-07-2001||07:41 PM||||Loki,<P>I have the same problem on my 88GT. For me, when I am around the 4000rmp range, I hear a tick, tick sound. I would think that if I had an exhaust leak, that I would hear it through the full RPM range. No?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DavidHenshaw||01-07-2001||09:47 PM||||If the car is "acting sluggish" starting at around 4,000 rpm I would suspect something is stopping up your exhaust system. Could it be the CAT converter? <P>I have a 750 cc Honda motorcycle. OK its not a car but its an internal combustion engine. Anyway it would not exceed 3,000 rpm. Turned out that one of the exhaust valves had slipped its adjustment and was not allowing the exhaust valve on this particular cylinder to open much. Under 3,000 rpm great power, but 3,000 rpm was a wall. After correcting the valve adjustment it would easily wind up to 8,000 rpm.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
